# Review: MarkdownPlugin

The core editor is solid and well covered: the `Document` type, the agent-facing `create`, `open` and
`update` operations, checkpoints/branches/merge (`versioning.test.ts`), suggestion branches
(`suggest-edit.test.ts`) and durable accept/reject (`accept-change.test.ts`, `reject-change.test.ts`)
all have tests. View modes persist per document through a ViewState aspect, the toolbar pulls
toolbar-disposition actions from the app graph, and `@` link queries and link-following exist, though
none of the UI paths is tested.

The biggest divergence is ownership. The spec describes `MarkdownArticle` driving the review model and
plugin-markdown contributing the `HistoryProvider`; in the code plugin-markdown only exposes an
`EditorBindingHook` socket, and plugin-review contributes the binding (version toolbar, ambient
suggestion overlay, Suggesting mode) and the `HistoryProvider`. The spec still names
`plugin-comments`, which no longer exists, and `MarkdownCapabilities.SuggestionSourcesProvider`,
which is not declared. Image upload is a toolbar dropzone button, not a drop onto the editor.

Several spec items share one fenced block (`VersionToolbar`, `VersionBanner`, the cards, the other
ops, `T-2` to `T-7`), and `deus review items` lists only the first item in each fence, so those items
are not judged here.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

